WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.300
-I had a great night
last night.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.467
I went out to, uh --
I went to Carbone.

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:05.701
-Ooh.
-Yeah.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:08.567
So I went with a my friend
Mike Birbiglia,

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:11.434
a very funny comedian, and we're
talking about stand-up,

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:12.968
and he's like -- he's like,
"Yeah, you should

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:15.300
do stand-up again."
And I go, yeah, I know,

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.868
because I did start my career
in stand-up, and I go,

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:21.501
I just haven't been on stage
in probably 10 years.

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:22.868
And, you know,
Chris Rock tells me

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:25.534
I should do stand-up again.
And I go, "Yeah, I know.

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:27.100
I just got to get an act
and blah, blah, blah."

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.601
He goes, "You should go
to the Comedy Cellar

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:30.200
and just go up," and I go,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.234
"I know, I know.
So I don't have an act."

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.667
And he's like,
"Let's just walk down there

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.601
and just -- just break
the ice of -- just the myth

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:39.467
of just going on stage
at the thing."

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:40.868
I go, "Yeah, okay."

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:43.834
So I went,
and it's an amazing club.

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:45.067
I go, "Yeah,
I totally remember it."

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.601
And you go down the stairs
and the whole thing,

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:50.067
and there's a great comedian,
Tina Friml, was on.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.267
So I went and watched her set.
It was awesome.

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:53.701
And then I go, "All right,
I'm gonna leave."

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:55.167
And I went in the hallway,
and Chris Rock

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.868
is sitting on the stairs.
He's like...

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:01.234
"I knew you'd come back.
I knew you'd come back.

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:02.801
You have to come back
to stand-up.

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.167
You've got to do it, man.
I knew it.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.734
I knew you'd come back."
I go -- and I felt

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.234
like the comedy gods
were just telling me,

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.567
like, "Yeah,
you should do stand-up again."

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.834
So I go, "Yeah."
I go, "Are you going up?"

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:13.801
And he's like, "Yeah,
maybe I'll go up."

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.434
So he surprised the audience.
Chris Rock gets up,

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:18.400
surprised the audience,
and destroys.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.734
He's unbelievable.

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:22.601
And so then I went up
to give him a bottle of water,

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:25.200
like as a goof,
and everyone started clapping.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.033
And then he goes, he took
the microphone, and he goes...

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:29.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.033
I was like, "Wow."

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:33.801
So I did stand-up
for the first time last night

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:35.300
in 10 years.
-Wow!

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:39.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:42.000
-It was unbelievable.
I totally remembered it.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.467
It was super fun.
It was great.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:45.634
I was like --
I don't even know --

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:46.767
I don't know what I was
talking about.

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:48.300
We just made it --
He made me so comfortable

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.467
up there.
But I remember, like,

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.868
"Oh, yeah,
it's so fun to be onstage."

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:55.367
And when a joke works,
the crowd loves it.

00:01:55.367 --> 00:01:57.968
I mean, like, the monologue.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.968 --> 00:01:59.734
-And when it doesn't.
-And when it doesn't work,

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:02.801
you know, it's silence,
and, uh...

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.667
No, but I do remember that.

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:07.100
The room gets hot, you know,

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.534
when you tell a good joke,
and then it's like...

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:10.100
And then it like,
comes down to room temperature.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.067
I loved it.
Anyways, I got the bug,

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.767
and I wanted
to thank -- thank Chris.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:16.367
Thanks, Mike.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:18.734
Thank you, Comedy Cellar.

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.434
I got to --
I'll work on an act.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:21.601
-Yeah.
-I'm gonna work on an act,

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:22.901
and I'll be out there,
because I want to go out

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:24.100
around the country.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.567
I want to say hi to everybody
and all the fans.

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.534
I love meeting people, and I
think it's gonna be fun.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.334
I'll do it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:30.801
So, it's Halloween.
Give me a couple months.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:31.968
I'll work on something.
-Couple months.

